      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108883",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that $X$ is a continuous random variable. For which of the following transformations can the change-of-variables method be applied to find the probability density function of $Y$?\n\n1. $Y = X^{2}$, where $X \u2208 (-1, 1)$\n2. $Y = 3 - 2X$, where $X \u2208 [2, 5]$\n3. $Y = e^{X}$, where $X \u2208 (- \u221e, \u221e)$"
